# The patients you never meet: opportunity cost as the hidden loser
next: {"title":"Where did this whole enterprise come from?","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/health-technology-assessment-deciding/where-did-this-whole-enterprise-come.cast"}

## A Yes Has a Payer
voice: female
level: basic

Over three parts we ask who actually pays when a health system says yes — and it starts with this bar: one year's health budget, fixed before anyone fell ill.
    text title "One year's health budget" x 500 y 620 font_size 30
    path bar_outline closed points [[120,420],[880,420],[880,500],[120,500]]
    label bar_label "Fixed before anyone fell ill" above #8f887c attach_to bar_outline

Beslutningsforum approves nusinersen for spinal muscular atrophy at an extraordinary price per patient. The bar does not grow to accommodate good news — so who pays for this slice?
    path yes_block closed #b5482e points [[120,420],[260,420],[260,500],[120,500]] style.fill #b5482e style.opacity 0.55
    label label_yes "Nusinersen — named patients" below #b5482e attach_to yes_block

    pause 1.8

An equal slice of care at the other end drops out of the budget: hip replacements, statin prescriptions, follow-up appointments that now simply do not happen.
    path displaced_block closed #c96567 points [[740,420],[880,420],[880,500],[740,500]] style.fill #c96567 style.opacity 0.55
    arrow arrow_out from.x 810 from.y 415 to.x 810 to.y 330
    label label_displaced "Hip replacements, statins, follow-ups — not delivered" below #c96567 attach_to arrow_out

The children who get the drug are named and photographed; the patients who paid for it never are, because nobody can say which ones they were.
    mark mark_displaced target label_displaced kind box
    delivery grave

## Doing the displacement arithmetic
voice: female
level: basic
use: equation_steps
with:
    title: The displacement arithmetic
    steps:
      - {tex: '\text{Budget} = 100\,000\,000\ \text{kr}', note: Fixed. Spent either way.}
      - {tex: '\frac{100\,000\,000\ \text{kr}}{3\,000\,000\ \text{kr/QALY}} \approx 33\ \text{QALYs}', note: Nusinersen}
      - {tex: '\frac{100\,000\,000\ \text{kr}}{100\,000\ \text{kr/QALY}} \approx 1\,000\ \text{QALYs}', note: Hip replacements}
      - {tex: '\Delta E = 33 - 1\,000 = -967\ \text{QALYs}', note: Health forgone}

    mark mark target step_3 kind box hidden true

    draw title

Now that we have seen that a yes always has a payer, let's do the payer's arithmetic: a hundred million kroner, which leaves the budget either way.
    draw step_0 note_0

At roughly three million kroner per QALY, nusinersen converts that budget into about thirty-three quality-adjusted life years.
    draw step_1 note_1

Same hundred million, spent instead on hip replacements at around a hundred thousand kroner per QALY — how many QALYs would that buy?

    pause 1.8

A thousand.
    draw step_2 note_2

So the yes costs nine hundred and sixty-seven QALYs of health that the same money would have bought elsewhere.
    draw step_3 note_3 mark

That loss is spread thinly over thousands of people who simply wait a little longer for a hip, and none of them will write to the newspaper, because none of them will ever learn it was them.
    highlight note_3 effect glow

## No budget cap, still a cost
voice: female
level: basic
use: decision_tree
with:
    root:
      id: choice
      type: decision
      label: 2 million kr, no budget cap
      children: [{label: Buy nusinersen, node: {id: drug, type: terminal, label: One patient-year of nusinersen, payoff: 0.4}}, {label: Buy hip replacements, node: {id: hips, type: terminal, label: About 20 hip replacements, payoff: 20}}]
    box:
      x: 40
      'y': 190
      w: 900
      h: 500
    unit: QALYs

Now that we have done the displacement arithmetic inside a fixed budget, meet a buyer with no budget cap at all: a private foundation spending two million kroner of its own money on nusinersen, buying roughly 0.4 QALYs.
    draw node_choice label_choice edge_choice_drug branchlabel_choice_drug node_drug label_drug payoff_drug

No public budget is touched, and nobody's operation is cancelled — so what does this yes cost?

    pause 1.8

The same two million would have bought about twenty hip replacements, and something like twenty QALYs — from an operation that has never once made the front page.
    draw edge_choice_hips branchlabel_choice_hips node_hips label_hips payoff_hips

So the loser is not a budget line but the health the money could have bought instead: opportunity cost lives in scarcity, not in the cap, and every yes — public or private — is judged against what it displaces.
    mark mark target payoff_hips kind box
    delivery grave

